      "content": "Data generally suggests that increasing the supply of *all* types of housing, including well-planned high- and moderate-density options, is the most effective strategy for increasing overall **affordability** in the long run by increasing the total available supply.\n\nRegarding **climate impact**, high-density, mixed-use development generally wins because it supports more efficient use of land and can drastically reduce the \"vein and artery\" of car travel, leading to lower per-capita carbon emissions from transportation.\n\nHowever, the \"winner\" depends on *how* the change is implemented, as poorly planned high-rises can have negative local impacts.",
