    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so it sounds like high density is basically the objectively better choice for the planet and for making housing cheaper then. if that's the case, why do you think people are still fighting so hard to keep single-family zoning? is it just about being \"NIMBY\" or is there an actual valid reason to keep things the way they are?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
